</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d992a66-b753-11f1-a88c-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-EN-Rubiks-Cube.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d992a66-b753-11f1-a88c-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-EN-Rubiks-Cube.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5e241570-b752-11f1-85bd-2d821a8b1802</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:26:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Trump ramps up his war on the media</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-trump-ramps-up-his-war-on-the-media</link><description>
US media outlets CNN, Politico and MS NOW are suing the Trump administration after it removed their press credentials and banned them from covering the White House. FRANCE 24 spoke to Steven Herman, executive director of the Jordan Center for Journalism Advocacy and Innovation at the University of Mississippi about the legality of the move and its wider ramnifications.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1e5ce1a-b395-11f1-972b-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-21T205608Z-444001983-RC283NA7GZ0I-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1e5ce1a-b395-11f1-972b-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-21T205608Z-444001983-RC283NA7GZ0I-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">689900b4-b74e-11f1-beae-31ca409dfa64</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:25:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Monte FRANCIS</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>UN General Assembly to discuss war, climate and AI</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-un-general-assembly-to-discuss-war-climate-and-ai</link><description>
World leaders are heading to New York for the world's biggest diplomatic gathering: the UN General Assembly. Throughout the week, attention will turn to the war in Iran, climate change and the race to rein in AI. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis and Theresa Squatrito from the London School of Economics discuss what to expect.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89fc3b28-b68a-11f1-96db-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-22T131132Z-811964852-RC2DONAIMQSV-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89fc3b28-b68a-11f1-96db-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-22T131132Z-811964852-RC2DONAIMQSV-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">59016f98-b74d-11f1-86a3-fd816f0fae6e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:20:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Monte FRANCIS</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UN General Assembly enters second day with key speeches ahead</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/un-general-assembly-enters-second-day-with-key-speeches-ahead</link><description>
It’s Day Two of the United Nations General Assembly in New York, with a packed programme including speeches by Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky. Some of the biggest names in artificial intelligence will also address the UN Security Council. France 24’s Jessica Le Masurier is covering the gathering for us.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1c2ae1c-b74d-11f1-a548-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-140159-140614-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1c2ae1c-b74d-11f1-a548-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-140159-140614-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b804ab54-b74d-11f1-bac6-f70b2fc2239a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:10:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>World leaders weigh AI worries, regulations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/world-leaders-weigh-ai-worries-regulations</link><description>
AI leaders are due to brief the UN Security Council at an emergency session later today. The meeting comes after weeks of warnings about the potentially uncontrollable risks posed by artificial intelligence. Delano D’Souza reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd7df5fe-b74d-11f1-b801-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-143902-144044-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd7df5fe-b74d-11f1-b801-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-143902-144044-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c2be455a-b74d-11f1-b60d-af7e98f82339</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:08:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Thomas Chatterton Williams on how Covid-19, George Floyd protests affected US social justice</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260923-thomas-chatterton-williams-on-how-covid-19-george-floyd-protests-affected-us-social-justice</link><description>
An acclaimed American author has spoken to FRANCE 24 about his theories on how American society's opinion and ideas of social justice have changed since the presidency of Barack Obama. Thomas Chatterton Williams says the left became disillusioned during Obama's second term, and in later years amid the George Floyd protests and Covid-19 pandemic the discourse shifted – initially for the left, but this also impacted the right. The ripples of those times are still resonating today. His latest book is entitled "Summer of Our Discontent: The Age of Certainty and the Demise of Discourse".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc91628c-b73e-11f1-8b47-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20097616816ab3b2c3c30703-89503864.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc91628c-b73e-11f1-8b47-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20097616816ab3b2c3c30703-89503864.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a563a84e-b72d-11f1-ac5b-e3a7bf7e3a71</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:40:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo XIV visit expected to boost Lourdes economy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-visit-expected-to-boost-lourdes-economy</link><description>
The town of Lourdes in southern France will be the second stop on Pope Leo XIV’s visit to the country, following his time in Paris. Around 150,000 people are expected to attend a mass led by the pontiff at the Sanctuary of Our Lady of Lourdes on Sunday. Local businesses are hoping the influx of visitors will also boost the economy, as pilgrims spend money on souvenirs, food and other goods. Our report by C. Neidhardt, C. Romain, E. Auriaux and C. Bénétreau.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9cb776b8-b745-11f1-940c-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-131635-131753-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9cb776b8-b745-11f1-940c-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-131635-131753-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a23b79ae-b745-11f1-acde-5f0db08195bd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:31:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Chinese beauty products prove resilient amid US-China trade war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/chinese-beauty-products-prove-resilient-amid-us-china-trade-war</link><description>
The US-China trade war has hit exports ranging from soybeans to solar panels, but one industry appears to be weathering the tariffs remarkably well. As Donald Trump and Xi Jinping prepare to meet in Washington this week, big-ticket exports are likely to be high on the agenda. But Chinese beauty products such as wigs, hair extensions and false eyelashes have proved highly resilient, with low prices and strong demand encouraging consumers to absorb the extra costs. China’s press-on nail industry, concentrated largely in one city, is also coming through the trade war without a scratch. Bryan Quinn
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/96a82182-b745-11f1-bff2-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-131214-131359-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/96a82182-b745-11f1-bff2-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-131214-131359-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c0928e2-b745-11f1-98ab-958b29f5e159</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:29:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel denounces Macron's UN remarks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-denounces-macron-s-un-remarks</link><description>
Israeli officials have hit back at French President Emmanuel Macron after he criticised Israel’s conduct in the occupied West Bank during his address to the UN General Assembly. But while Macron used strong words against Israel, France allowed Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s plane to fly through French airspace on its way to New York, despite an ICC arrest warrant against him. Delano D’Souza reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f9be0b0-b744-11f1-92a6-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-130719-130913-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f9be0b0-b744-11f1-92a6-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-130719-130913-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8572b75c-b744-11f1-9d71-cd03806d7a8a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:56:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>China cracks down on scam centres in neighbouring Myanmar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260923-china-cracks-down-on-scam-centres-in-neighbouring-myanmar</link><description>
In Southeast Asia, hundreds of thousands of people working in fraud centres are scamming people across the world. US authorities suggest the fraudsters are responsible for scams worth almost $10 billion a year against US nationals alone. Victims in Europe, the UK and China have also been targeted. Human rights groups further warn that those working in the centres are often themselves victims of human trafficking – forced to work as slaves.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c1b295e-b6b4-11f1-9b6c-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-FRZ-CHINE-SCAM-CENTERS-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c1b295e-b6b4-11f1-9b6c-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-FRZ-CHINE-SCAM-CENTERS-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3307b926-b6b4-11f1-a438-f368beefaef0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:01:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jan CAMENZIND BROOMBY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>When climate mitigation becomes politicised: The Guardian uncovers IPCC links to Saudi oil industry</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260923-when-climate-mitigation-becomes-political-the-guardian-uncovers-ipcc-links-to-saudi-oil-industry</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Eoghan Gilmartin, an award-winning investigative journalist and part of The Guardian team whose investigation examined links between IPCC authors and Saudi Arabia’s oil industry, including Saudi Aramco. Their findings take us to the intersection of climate science, political and economic interests, and institutional credibility, and into the politically consequential terrain of climate mitigation: how societies decide to respond to climate change.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/feb1f334-b72c-11f1-a58b-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-183050-184157-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/feb1f334-b72c-11f1-a58b-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-183050-184157-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">019bfa30-b73d-11f1-9038-4518c6baa669</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:53:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hurricane Polo churns off Mexico</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/hurricane-polo-churns-off-mexico</link><description>
Hurricane Polo has strengthened into one of the most powerful Pacific cyclones in decades and is expected to skirt Mexico’s southwestern coast as a Category 5 storm. The Miami-based National Hurricane Center described Polo as an “extremely dangerous” storm, with maximum sustained winds of 165 miles per hour.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b514b590-b73b-11f1-ba3f-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120802-120947-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b514b590-b73b-11f1-ba3f-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120802-120947-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">baf4e75a-b73b-11f1-8a98-dda56df48f1c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:49:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia attacks four Ukrainian regions overnight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-attacks-four-ukrainian-regions-overnight</link><description>
Ukrainian authorities say Russia attacked at least four regions overnight with missiles and drones, killing at least five people. Ukrainian forces meanwhile damaged another Russian oil refinery in a long-range strike. The attacks came as President Volodymyr Zelensky met US President Donald Trump in New York for talks on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly. Camille Knight reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/876bd222-b73b-11f1-86e7-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120559-120740-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/876bd222-b73b-11f1-86e7-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120559-120740-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d9ac37e-b73b-11f1-bad1-9133db15b5ac</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:48:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US President warns Tehran at UN but says talks ongoing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-warns-tehran-at-un-but-says-talks-ongoing</link><description>
The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani shares further insights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f81f8c8-b73b-11f1-9bbb-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120230-120511-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f81f8c8-b73b-11f1-9bbb-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120230-120511-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">55615c0c-b73b-11f1-9c18-79ae88c1a4dc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:46:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Shame': Macron slams Trump's Gaza diplomacy in final UN speech</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-shame-macron-slams-trump-s-gaza-diplomacy-in-final-un-speech</link><description>
🇫🇷 French President Emmanuel Macron criticised Gaza diplomacy at the UN General Assembly, calling it a "shameful spectacle" and urging action to reopen humanitarian routes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86721a2a-b73b-11f1-b986-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/thumbnail-macron.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86721a2a-b73b-11f1-b986-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/thumbnail-macron.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef32bba6-b73a-11f1-babe-9dffa8ffd555</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:38:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Fresh drilling for a lost Egyptian queen?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260923-fresh-drilling-for-a-lost-egyptian-queen</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, September 23: The papers look ahead to US President Donald Trump hosting his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping. In other news, a Haitian-born novelist, tipped to win France's prestigious Goncourt literary prize, has been struck by an AI scandal. Finally, could the remains of Nefertiti lie behind the burial chamber of Tutankhamun?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08d13544-b734-11f1-8a41-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11277582616ab3a099842097-24370801.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08d13544-b734-11f1-8a41-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11277582616ab3a099842097-24370801.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a57e5b0c-b733-11f1-bf1d-275c8639cafe</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:31:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Antonia KERRIGAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>ICC convicts Central African Republic rebel leader of crimes against humanity</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260923-icc-convicts-central-african-republic-rebel-leader-of-crimes-against-humanity</link><description>
The International Criminal Court on Wednesday convicted former Central African Republic militia commander Mahamat Said Abdel Kani of torture and unlawful imprisonment. Said oversaw a detention centre in the capital Bangui infamous for its brutal conditions during the country's sectarian civil war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/637d92bc-b739-11f1-9542-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/2d99e0625dca081335e504ec5a5c72cc00ec52cd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/637d92bc-b739-11f1-9542-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/2d99e0625dca081335e504ec5a5c72cc00ec52cd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">643f3d68-b739-11f1-a8b0-4168c612c23b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:27:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/637d92bc-b739-11f1-9542-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/2d99e0625dca081335e504ec5a5c72cc00ec52cd.jpg">© Remko de Waal, ANP via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Live: Syria’s Sharaa vows that Israeli-occupied Golan Heights will remain Syrian</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war</link><description>
Syria’s President Ahmed al-Sharaa insisted at the UN Wednesday that the Golan Heights region will remain Syrian after Colombia’s new far-right government last month recognised Israeli sovereignty over the occupied territory. The United Nations considers the strategically important region as Syrian territory under Israeli military occupation. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
